[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6197245830","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124508#issuecomment-6197245830","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124508","id":6197245830,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABcWJ3hg","user":{"login":"skorpnok","id":6632336,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzIzMzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6632336?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok","html_url":"https://github.com/skorpnok","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-15T16:40:05Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T16:41:34Z","body":"No worries, you know more about this than I do. Probably faster and easier if you make a PR. Does destroying the token after it has been commited, really cancel it? What about when on_done is already in progress when the destruction of the token occurs? In my testing the on_done and window_destroy functions were running seemingly parallel to each other. I feel like this would also just minimize the time window for a race condition.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6197245830/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6197361045","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124508#issuecomment-6197361045","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124508","id":6197361045,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABcWQ5lQ","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-15T16:45:57Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T16:49:44Z","body":"> Does destroying the token after it has been commited, really cancel it?\r\n\r\nIt might not, but it doesn't matter. AFAIK once an object is destroyed it becomes a \"zombie\" that no-ops requests and events to avoid any further race. In fact, in the \"after\" dump the `done` event gets marked discarded.\r\n\r\nI haven't worked much on libwayland so TIWAGOS. The only reason I know this is because of the embedder. I've seen _things_ xD\r\n\r\nEdit:\r\n\r\n> Probably faster and easier if you make a PR.\r\n\r\nForgot to say, I'll do! Once again thank you for looking into it in the first place and for your patience.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6197361045/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6197448945","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124508#issuecomment-6197448945","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124508","id":6197448945,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABcWWQ8Q","user":{"login":"skorpnok","id":6632336,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzIzMzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6632336?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok","html_url":"https://github.com/skorpnok","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-15T16:50:24Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T16:50:24Z","body":"Aight I'll close this then, cheers!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6197448945/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6198497654","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124508#issuecomment-6198497654","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124508","id":6198497654,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABcXWRdg","user":{"login":"skorpnok","id":6632336,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzIzMzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6632336?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok","html_url":"https://github.com/skorpnok","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-15T17:44:34Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T17:44:48Z","body":"@deralmas  I checked the libwayland source and you are right with the \"zombies\" thing. It just consumes all pending events in that case. I still think that since the event polling thread is a separate thread from where window_destroy is called there is a _very very slim_ chance the token and the surface get destroyed after on_done was emitted but before the call to activate but it's probably not worth worrying about. Thanks for the extra explanation!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6198497654/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6201629713","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124508#issuecomment-6201629713","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124508","id":6201629713,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABcaVcEQ","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-15T20:29:15Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T20:29:15Z","body":"> I still think that since the event polling thread is a separate thread from where window_destroy is called there is a very very slim chance the token and the surface get destroyed after on_done was emitted but before the call to activate but it's probably not worth worrying about.\r\n\r\nI don't think that's actually an issue. The Wayland thread is a... thread, yes, but the event loop has actually got a mutex (which is why we have our own weird custom event loop logic), so either it gets destroyed, thus turning the token proxy into a \"zombie\" (with all that entails) or it handles the done event and then the window gets instantly destroyed.\r\n\r\nIt's hard to see cause the mutex is locked _outside_ of the WaylandThread calls. Frankly I kinda regret doing that especially as the default lock is recursive. That said, if you look at the DisplayServer callers of `DisplayServerWayland::_delete_window`, you'll see that they lock the event loop manually.\r\n\r\nThe only thing I've always been somewhat concerned about is the `wl_display_roundtrip` situation. IIRC it's actually a custom event loop of its own and thus it can handle events in the main thread. We also abuse roundtrip in general somewhat as frankly I should have used sync (and waited for successful handling in a better way) instead but oh well, it all works somehow in the end xD\r\n\r\n> Thanks for the extra explanation!\r\n\r\nMy pleasure! I could talk about this for hours haha","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6201629713/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]